        "uuid": "05d0140a_78c98b96",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T09:05:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we really want to go the route of maintaining multiple versions of microdroid kernel? We don\u0027t do this for GKI, why should we do it for microdroid?\n\nThis also goes against go/android-userdebug-policy",
      "parentUuid": "53b4b2b4_9afa4127",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "ae48ed0c27534dea0f98c0d77d19ed7a73eee86f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "94e657e4_62f0afa1",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T09:06:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Previously Will was against having multiple separate microdroid kernels. If possible, I\u0027d prefer if we wait for him to come back from the vacation and share his thoughts on this",
      "parentUuid": "05d0140a_78c98b96",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "ae48ed0c27534dea0f98c0d77d19ed7a73eee86f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ffa76ef_9d23740c",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T09:11:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You were in the meeting with Sandeep, right? I am not happy with this either, but it was a product decision, wasn\u0027t it? I don\u0027t think it\u0027s wise to delay anything further at this moment. \n\nLet\u0027s land this first, and think about how we can handle this situation. Reverting it later is also in the options.",
      "parentUuid": "94e657e4_62f0afa1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "ae48ed0c27534dea0f98c0d77d19ed7a73eee86f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4c7e84ed_91ee1004",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-22T13:20:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e You were in the meeting with Sandeep, right?\n\nI had a meeting right after, so I guess I missed the part when this was decided.\n\nI am not going to block you, just voicing my opinion that this decision is influenced by a rush for small win immediately, and will bite us back (most likely in a very short term).",
      "parentUuid": "8ffa76ef_9d23740c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "ae48ed0c27534dea0f98c0d77d19ed7a73eee86f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0852c207_88b553c9",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 13,
      "author": {
        "id": 1572468
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-28T11:31:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is a really bad idea but as long as there\u0027s an understanding that we can ignore any bug reports from this config, then I can live with it (because I will simply ignore it). In other words, if you choose to use this config, you\u0027re on your own if it goes wrong. However, I don\u0027t understand what that means for CI and test coverage.\n\nWho will be responsible for maintaining kernel images built from this config?",
      "parentUuid": "4c7e84ed_91ee1004",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 52
      },
